  "core_obligations": [
    "After the named large-parameter calculus, boundary/interior Garding and perfect-elliptic input, general fourth-order LS operators cannot simply be imposed on each second-order factor. The authors first build loss-free control of all four boundary traces using the graded complete family and eliminate its auxiliary Ej terms, while separately deriving Dirichlet single-factor estimates with half loss confined to real-root regions. A common phase-space cone and the two-sided tau/sigma window keep the two loss regions apart; the ordered factor concatenation, commutators and D_d^k Lambda^(2-k) lift then recover the full fourth-order norm with only one half loss. The final lower-order absorption closes the general-boundary estimate. These mutually constrained trace/model/parameter-concatenation stages form one H3 unit; the last sum of inequalities alone, terminology and downstream decay are not the grade basis.",
